{"title":"2025 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b1d4863ff0b5eadb4bca7ad84560c55f63976c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal R$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> is divided into a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef76e1d390ab024a1cf20b896e56cf8ff425a2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of finitely many smaller rectangles with sides parallel to the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b1d4863ff0b5eadb4bca7ad84560c55f63976c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal R$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> such that no three rectangles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef76e1d390ab024a1cf20b896e56cf8ff425a2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> share a common corner. An ant is initially located at the bottom-left corner of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b1d4863ff0b5eadb4bca7ad84560c55f63976c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal R$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />. In one operation, we can choose a rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd21bd21a7e5acc5a201ef1840109c0efc62803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\in \\mathcal S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> such that the ant is currently located at one of the corners of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and move the ant to one of the two corners of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> adjacent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>Suppose that after a finite number of operations, the ant ends up at the top-right corner of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b1d4863ff0b5eadb4bca7ad84560c55f63976c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal R$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that some rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd21bd21a7e5acc5a201ef1840109c0efc62803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\in \\mathcal S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> was chosen in at least two operations.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032600\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 69/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 447/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2132/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.248      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    6.248      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36120:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018032600 and revision id 283650. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}